printing an [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]actionable error that tells the agent exactly how to rewrite it, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]while staying lenient enough that legitimate subjects, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]merge/revert/fixup subjects, and projects that opt out are never [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]blocked.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202607/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]conventional_commit_subject_gate.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-bj[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-bj/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Conventional-subject grammar in the Rust core[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core_grammar[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core_grammar: add a pure `commit_subject` domain module to sase-core [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that parses a commit subject into type/scope/breaking/description, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]classifies exemptions, and reports a stable violation code; expose it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through the `sase_core_py` binding.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Python facade, policy config, and shared header helper[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]python_surface[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core_grammar[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]python_surface: add the typed Python facade over the new binding, the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`commit.message` configuration block with its schema and defaults, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]retarget the existing init-memory conventional-header check at the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]shared helper.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Reject invalid subjects in CommitWorkflow[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]commit_enforcement[dim] · [dim][/dim]after python_surface[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]commit_enforcement: gate `CommitWorkflow.run()` on the subject policy [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]before any side effect runs, render the actionable rejection message, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]record the telemetry reason, and update the existing tests that commit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with non-conventional messages.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Document the gate and guard against type-list drift[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs_and_guidance[dim] · [dim][/dim]after commit_enforcement[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs_and_guidance: document the new configuration and the rejection [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]behavior, mention the gate in the git commit skill, and add a regression[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]test that keeps the repo's PR-title CI type list compatible with the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]validator defaults.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-bj","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","phase_bead_id":"sase-bj.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-2e242933022577063cd9ea5fc6df6b08","started_at":"2026-07-31T11:15:09.325800+00:00","state":"active"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1785499548,"sha":"748b617c0b060a20861331e8b65b6d3725fbcf44","subject":"feat(commit): add commit subject validation policy"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"9126785371bae8c8db22e57b4be98ac867c618137bf61641a08521d3fd2a389b","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-bj.2/chat.md","size_bytes":23963},"commits":{"digest":"1fbead1d945a03304e8b16048cd82ef2c0e1558aa41e63e04489c1058ecf5893","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-bj.2/commits